1
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,980
Something will work out.

2
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without work, come to me.

3
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,500
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:11,560
Look, the steel is burning too.

5
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:23,500
You understand, right? Yeah, yeah, I get it.

7
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,400
Once you understand, just follow me quietly.

8
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,560
Isn't this Ryo-chan's leave request?

9
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,980
He's taking tomorrow off?

10
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,160
Ah

11
00:01:56,740 --> 00:01:58,680
Ryo-san, who always takes
days off without permission,

12
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,960
actually bothering to file a leave request?

13
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:03,360
Senpai, what could be going on?

14
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:11,340
Right, it's intriguing. Today is March 2nd,
so tomorrow must be March 3rd

15
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:13,680
Hinamatsuri

16
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:20,700
Right, the Peach Festival. But I feel like March
3rd had something else besides the Hina dolls.

17
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:24,460
Come to think of it... yes, I think so.

18
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:29,580
Ryo-chan's birthday is March 3rd, isn't it?

19
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:30,940
That's right.

20
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:32,140
Right.

21
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:34,800
You were born on Girls' Day, Ryo-san.

22
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,860
It would've been perfect
if you'd been a girl.

23
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:42,120
Don't gleefully bring up something
people are sensitive about.

24
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:42,920
Sorry.

25
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,540
By the way, Senpai.

26
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:48,620
Nothing good ever happens on your March 3rd birthday,
does it?

27
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:50,200
Yeah, that's right, I think.

28
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:52,700
Four years ago, on March 3rd,

29
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:55,340
you went to guard a
500-million-yen set of Hina dolls.

30
00:02:58,340 --> 00:03:02,320
Didn't he get knocked over by a big
dump truck while on patrol two years ago?

31
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:08,200
And last year, there was that gas
explosion at the police box, right?

32
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:15,880
That's not all. Ever since he was born, something
terrible has happened to him every March 3rd without fail.

33
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:20,600
But what does that have to
do with taking paid leave?

34
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:25,220
Ever since he became a police officer, he's
often had terrible things happen on the job too.

35
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,900
That way, the chances of something
terrible happening will be lower.

36
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:31,560
Hiding at home won't do any good, you know.

37
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:32,980
That's right, senpai.

38
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:35,660
As long as nothing terrible happens to me,
that's all that matters.

39
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:37,060
R-really?

40
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:38,260
Well then,

41
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,100
I suppose there's nothing we can do.

42
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:43,100
Anyway, no matter what huge
incident happens tomorrow,

43
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,820
I'm not stepping out of the house.

44
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,840
Make sure you tell the Chief that too.

45
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:55,740
What? Ryotsu's off today?

46
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:58,120
He did file his leave
request properly, though.

47
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,820
I see. But that's a problem.

48
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,200
Chief, is something wrong?

49
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:07,840
Well, it's nothing major,
but I need to see Ryotsu about something.

50
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:11,960
Ryo-san said he'd be home all day today.

51
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:15,600
If you have business with him,
why don't you visit him directly?

52
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,820
Yes. I'll do that.

53
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:22,720
AV equipment you no longer need

54
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:24,760
Don't you have any computers or the like?

55
00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:28,320
It's fine even if the AV
equipment doesn't work.

56
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,260
It's always the same here.

57
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:32,820
So noisy! I can't sleep like this!

58
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:34,640
Damn it, I'm going to go complain!

59
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:37,640
AV equipment that broke down at home

60
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:38,080
Come to think of it,

61
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,520
something similar happened on
March 3rd ten years ago too.

62
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,860
the loudspeaker from the paper
exchange truck was so noisy

63
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:46,440
when I went to complain,

64
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:48,680
some guy was tossing
his cigarette butts away

65
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:51,220
and I nearly burned the whole place down.

66
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:56,000
Yeah, I've decided I
won't go out at all today.

67
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:58,260
Feel free to just sleep quietly.

68
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,760
This is the Tokyo Metropolitan
public relations van.

69
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:06,680
There have been recent burglary incidents.

70
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:09,000
Be sure to call out to
someone before you head out.

71
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,280
Dokkoi Pro Wrestling, the second-ranked wrestler in Kyushu,
has been spotted in Kameari.

72
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:15,820
Yokanise, the first-ever Sakurajima Drop!

73
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:17,200
Will Tokyo strike back?

74
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:19,760
The nationwide miracle Dodeth Battle...

75
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,440
Now, that shows what lies ahead.

76
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,220
For your family...

77
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:25,440
Can't you just sleep?

78
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,720
Alright, time for a game.

79
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:37,780
It's me, Ohara.

80
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:40,340
Still sleeping, Ryotsu?

81
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:44,320
For the chief to come all the way here,
it must be something serious.

82
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:48,760
But I don't recall doing anything
to anger the chief lately.

83
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:49,480
Ryotsu!

84
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,940
I know you're in there, so open up already!

85
00:05:53,220 --> 00:05:56,560
I'm angry! What on earth did you do?

86
00:05:56,560 --> 00:06:03,740
Come to think of it, on March 3rd five years ago,
Terai's careless mistake

87
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:09,400
was mistaken for mine, and I had to
pull a tire in a Tokyo-wide marathon

88
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:12,080
wasn't I?
Surely it's not going to happen again?

89
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:16,240
It's not locked? I'm coming in.

90
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:19,440
This is ridiculous. Getting scolded
for something I don't remember doing.

91
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,720
Once in a while, Ryotsu...

92
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,360
Is he not here?

93
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:27,420
It can't be helped.

94
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:28,180
I'll kill some time outside.

95
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:30,820
Close call, close call.

96
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:35,200
That was March 3rd,
back in my third year of high school.

97
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:40,180
I carelessly went outside in my underwear,
drinking milk,

98
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:43,280
and got mistaken for a pervert
lurking around the neighborhood.

99
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,780
and got chased relentlessly by the cops.

100
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:53,240
Before I knew it,
I'd been charged with about twenty murders.

101
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,480
Yeah, I can't go out looking like this.

102
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,180
I'm borrowing these for a bit.

103
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:03,280
Damn, these are Aunt Ryo's clothes,
aren't they?

104
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:07,000
Oh well,
I'll head to the station like this for now.

105
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,080
Guess I'll borrow some
clothes from Sensō-ji, then.

106
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:36,680
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

107
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,940
Cobra Twist!

108
00:07:38,820 --> 00:07:39,900
Zigzag Low!

109
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:42,280
Space Triple Kick!

110
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,420
I've been beaten to a pulp before.

111
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,580
Let's wait until practice is over.

112
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:59,880
It's oddly tidy today.

113
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:05,120
Well, let's wait here until
Sakonji's practice ends.

114
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,460
Oof, there we go.

115
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:11,362
Haah...

116
00:08:11,412 --> 00:08:27,220
Today's practice was tough, wasn't it?

117
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:31,660
If you're giving up at that level, you
won't be able to handle violent criminals.

118
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:33,060
Haa, it's hot.

119
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:35,580
Someone's here.

120
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:38,200
It's probably the cleaning lady.

121
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,180
She seems to be asleep,
so let's leave her be.

122
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:41,880
Yeah.

123
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,120
Man, I'm all sweaty and sticky.

124
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,160
Me too.

125
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:52,240
This is...

126
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:02,820
But why are Komachi and the
others in the men's changing room?

127
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:07,260
Wasn't it March 3rd of the
year they came to the precinct?

128
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:09,580
If I happened to trip and fall
at the bottom of the stairs,

129
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:13,880
I'd be branded a lecherous cop.

130
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,280
You saw that, didn't you?

131
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:19,020
and got beaten to a pulp.

132
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,800
If anyone sees me dressed like this,
in a place like this...

133
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,360
That won't be the end of it.

134
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,380
I have to get out of here as fast as I can.

135
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:31,800
Shower first, okay?

136
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:32,340
Okay!

137
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:36,540
Auntie

138
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:40,040
It seems the drain pipe is clogged.

139
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,360
Could you take a look?

140
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:44,340
Well, I have an urgent matter...

141
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:47,620
Come on, you were napping just a moment ago.

142
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:48,540
It'll only take a second.

143
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:49,260
Stop it!

144
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:53,340
Kyaa! It's a man!

145
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:56,620
No, wait!

146
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:57,680
No, no!

147
00:09:59,020 --> 00:09:59,600
Aaaaaah!

148
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:04,520
Hakkun! Where did that man go?

149
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:06,140
Kokomachi!

150
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:08,160
Eeeeeeh!

151
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:16,040
Hehehe, tat-tat-tat-tat! Heh.

152
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:22,040
Damn, I can't wear this outfit anymore.
Sorry, auntie.

153
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,840
Lucky! There are spare clothes.

154
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,200
This one's nice.

155
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,340
I wonder if it belonged
to some biker gang member.

156
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,840
Speaking of biker gangs,

157
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:38,420
that was March 3rd,
back when I was a first-year in high school.

158
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:42,220
I borrowed a leather jacket that a senior of
my friend's older brother had supposedly worn,

159
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:43,940
and I was walking around town

160
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:51,080
when I got caught up in
a fight between biker gangs

161
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,400
and ended up getting arrested.

162
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:57,060
If I wear something like this, I'm
bound to get into another lousy situation.

163
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:04,600
This is the most decent one.

164
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:08,520
With this,
there's no way I'll get arrested by mistake.

165
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:13,660
It's fine, right?

166
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:23,620
Of all things, why is a group of riot police

167
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:28,300
I knew March 3rd would
bring nothing but trouble.

168
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:34,360
Hey, what's going on here?

169
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:38,180
Well, it's a special training
for welcoming new recruits,

170
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:40,600
so we're running a marathon
all the way to the Edogawa River.

171
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,900
Didn't they explain this at the start?

172
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:45,680
Something about a special
training for new recruits...

173
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:50,460
This is the Demon 99th Mobile Unit.

174
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:57,720
The 99th Mobile Unit, famed as the strongest in
Tokyo for its harsh training and iron discipline.

175
00:11:57,720 --> 00:12:03,360
But many members are said to drop out,
unable to keep up with the brutal training.

176
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:06,920
No way, I'm not putting up with that lot!

177
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:07,620
Yeah!

178
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:11,180
Hey, you there, rookie!

179
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:13,340
Yeah, you!

180
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:16,200
What is this?

181
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:18,680
Don't you try to run away!

182
00:12:19,180 --> 00:12:20,580
Dabisumonikusu!

183
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:26,480
Skipping out on the new recruit welcome training?
You've got some nerve.

184
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,960
I'm not a riot police officer!

185
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:29,960
What did you say?

186
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:33,100
Anyone can see you're 100% riot police,
so don't give me that!

187
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:34,780
Or is it something else?

188
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:36,620
Are you a comedian from
some riot police skit?

189
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:39,900
You're not some cosplay-obsessed riot police nerd,
are you?

190
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:43,440
I'm a proper, certified police officer!

191
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,520
But I didn't become a cop
just to join the riot police!

192
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:50,780
That's what almost
everyone assigned here says.

193
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:51,880
But...

194
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:55,720
From today,
you're a member of the 99th Riot Unit!

195
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,760
Do you think whining like
that will get you anywhere?

196
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:01,900
Stop your jabbering and
get back in line, now!

197
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:09,620
No good, it doesn't look like
anything I say will get through.

198
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:13,240
In that case,
I'll have to slip past him and run.

199
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:18,400
Come to think of it, back when I was
still at the police academy, on March 3rd,

200
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:22,240
I happened to be watching
another squad's training,

201
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:24,900
and the instructor
mistook me for one of them,

202
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:27,420
and forced me to join the training.

203
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:29,680
When I tried to run away,

204
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:33,280
I was made to run five
times as far as the others,

205
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:38,400
and taken all the way to Mount Hakkoda,
where snow still lingered.

206
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:41,440
On top of that, they had me do a solo duty.

207
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:47,540
Once tomorrow comes,
the misunderstanding will be cleared up.

208
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:50,360
I just have to put up with it for one day.

209
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:54,620
It's better than defying them
and getting into serious trouble.

210
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:56,920
I want to go.

211
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,420
Left there.

212
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:19,460
Captain, why do you make us run
through such weird places all the time?

213
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:22,660
We are the riot police who
protect the capital's public order.

214
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:26,420
Criminals sometimes hide in places like this,
you know.

215
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:27,640
Understood?

216
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:29,860
Yes, sir, understood.

217
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:38,160
Hey, pull yourselves together!

218
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:40,720
Listen, if anyone drops out,

219
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:42,960
everyone starts over from
the beginning, got it?

220
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:45,180
Damn, there's no choice.

221
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:52,920
Is this any time to be resting?

222
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,900
Next, swim from here

223
00:14:54,900 --> 00:14:56,580
to the far bank and back.

224
00:14:57,760 --> 00:15:01,220
Everyone, swim with 20-kilo
backpacks and iron geta on!

225
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,940
Such an absurd...

226
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:05,940
What if the suspect is a strong swimmer?

227
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:10,540
If you don't train with this kind of handicap all the time,
you won't stand a chance!

228
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:12,340
Understood!

229
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,140
Ready?

230
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:16,040
Alright, jump in!

231
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,360
Jump in!

232
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:22,100
Let's finish this training
quickly and head back to the dorm!

233
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,960
What are you doing! You idiots!

234
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:30,380
If even one of you drops out,
we start over from the beginning!

235
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,460
Hurry up and swim!

236
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:35,400
Nobody's keeping up!

237
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:38,180
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

238
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,180
Alright, grab onto me!

239
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,860
You're next!

240
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:53,000
That guy's pretty good.

241
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,780
Now, we'll begin the next training exercise.

242
00:15:57,240 --> 00:16:00,120
You'll stop an enemy charging at
you by putting your body on the line.

243
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,680
Your opponent will be that.

244
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:06,720
Are we stopping a car with our bare hands?

245
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:10,220
Criminals often use cars
to make their getaway.

246
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:12,080
What good are you if you
can't manage that much?

247
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,700
Normally, nobody can do it.

248
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,840
Do you think we don't know that?

249
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:18,420
If you fail, you'll start over
from the beginning, got it?

250
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:20,160
Alright, go!

251
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:41,700
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

252
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:42,900
Next is that one.

253
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:48,780
Sevennn!

254
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:50,120
Whoa!

255
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:52,820
Wow, that's incredible!

256
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:58,940
Alright, if it comes to this,
I'll stop the dog too.

257
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:06,880
Whoa!

258
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,260
Whoa!

259
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:08,580
Whoa!

260
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:08,820
Whoa!

261
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:09,900
Whoa!

262
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:13,240
Whoa!

263
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:34,660


264
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:35,840
We've got a dispatch request.

265
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:39,420
A bomb-obsessed man has barricaded
himself in an office building.

266
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:40,960
Right, understood.

267
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:43,000
Training is cancelled.

268
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:45,620
Rookies,
return to the barracks and stand by.

269
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:48,760
Phew, finally off the hook.

270
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:52,820
But Ryotsu,
you're coming with us to join the main unit.

271
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,660
Me?

272
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:56,900
No more whining, just come along!

273
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:10,600
Don't come near me!
If you come any closer, this won't end well!

274
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:13,980
Calm down! What do you want?

275
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,220
I told you not to come!

276
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:19,631
This bomb, you know,
can take out one or two buildings like this

277
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:21,680
with no trouble at all!

278
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:24,200
Seems you're pretty worked up.

279
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:28,760
Chief, I hear the 99th Riot
Unit is heading this way.

280
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:32,260
The fearsome 99th Riot Unit

281
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,360
Sorry to keep you waiting.

282
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,500
That's...

283
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:41,700
The 99th Riot Unit,
guardians of the capital's peace.

284
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:43,200
We've arrived!

285
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,460
With resolve...

286
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:52,760
Why are Komachi and the others here?

287
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:55,140
Thank you for your hard work.

288
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:59,800
From here,
please leave it to the 99th Riot Unit.

289
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:04,700
The Chief's here too.
We'd better stay as far away as possible.

290
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:07,020
Now, I'll give the operational orders.

291
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:12,100
The first squad will attempt to breach the front.
But this is a diversion.

292
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:17,660
The second squad, which I command, will breach
through the back entrance and secure the suspect.

293
00:19:17,660 --> 00:19:19,480
The rest will stand by here.

294
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,500
As for me...

295
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:24,080
Standby.
Support the initial response riot police.

296
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:29,980
Ryo-san, if you keep wandering around here,
the Chief and Komachi will spot you!

297
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:31,800
Shit.

298
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:35,380
Captain,
please let me join the assault team too.

299
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:36,100
What?

300
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:40,500
I didn't join the riot police
to sit idle at the back.

301
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:43,400
I joined to put my own body on
the line and protect the citizens.

302
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:46,180
I want to do my job on the front line.

303
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,580
Ryotsu, you...

304
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:54,220
Get behind my back.

305
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:55,840
Yes, thank you.

306
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:57,620
Looks like we're really going to do it now.

307
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:09,380
Squad 2 has reached the back entrance.

308
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:11,480
Squad 1 begins the diversion.

309
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,580
Move in!

310
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:16,080
They're coming, they're coming!

311
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:24,920
Grumbling and complaining...

312
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:44,200
Whaaaaat?

313
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:46,420
Yay, we did it!

314
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:48,640
As expected of the 99th Riot Unit!

315
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,480
Hey, fold these! Hurry up and fold them!

316
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:58,180
Right, while I have the chance...

317
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:01,660
Good thing there's a locker room right here.

318
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:05,880
I'll borrow some other clothes
and make my exit from here.

319
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:11,940
Yikes! It's a time bomb!

320
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:16,640
He actually really planted it.

321
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:19,620
And there's only three minutes left!

322
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:22,020
In that case, the only option
is to cut the cord and stop it.

323
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:24,100
Cut the right one, cut the right one.

324
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:29,140
So which is it, red or blue?

325
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:31,500
Red it is.

326
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:35,780
Wait, now that I think about it, on March
3rd in my sixth year of elementary school,

327
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:38,540
when I was asked whether I
wanted the red or the blue candy,

328
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,880
I asked my old man, and I ate the red one,

329
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:43,505
and it was a super spicy candy,

330
00:21:43,555 --> 00:21:46,920
and afterward my mouth swelled up so badly I couldn't even eat anything,
remember?

331
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:49,240
Alright, this time it's blue.

332
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,600
It got faster!

333
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:56,960
What am I supposed to do?

334
00:21:59,540 --> 00:22:00,340
That's it!

335
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:12,660
We should be safe once we get this far.

336
00:22:28,840 --> 00:22:30,680
Were there other bombs?

337
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:33,100
But who on earth

338
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,460
Where is Ryotsu?

339
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:36,360
Well,

340
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,540
Captain.

341
00:22:38,960 --> 00:22:40,920
Anyway, this Ryotsu guy,

342
00:22:53,820 --> 00:22:56,060
every entrance was under surveillance,

343
00:22:56,460 --> 00:22:58,620
and apparently no one came out.

344
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,580
Did he vanish into thin air?

345
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:03,300
Ryotsu.

346
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:05,280
Maybe he was

347
00:23:05,940 --> 00:23:07,820
sent to solve this case

348
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,820
by the gods themselves.

349
00:23:11,320 --> 00:23:11,980
A story like this

350
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:14,280
no one will believe, I suppose.

351
00:23:14,860 --> 00:23:18,020
Let's keep it quietly in our hearts.

352
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:19,020
Yes.

353
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:22,460
We're back.

354
00:23:23,020 --> 00:23:24,280
Thank you for your hard work.

355
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:26,100
By the way, Reiko.

356
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:28,100
Did you manage to get in touch with Ryotsu?

357
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:29,620
No, not yet.

358
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:30,820
I see.

359
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:35,540
My grandson Daisuke made a birthday present for Ryotsu,
so

360
00:23:35,540 --> 00:23:37,640
I was hoping to give it to him.

361
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,200
How cute.

362
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:43,140
Ryo-san isn't at home either.
I wonder where on earth he went.

363
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:46,760
Maybe he's alone somewhere
no one can reach him.

364
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:47,920
Yeah, I suppose.

365
00:23:54,940 --> 00:23:57,640
After all that hard work,
this is how it ends again

366
00:23:57,640 --> 00:24:00,600
That's why I hate March 3rd.

367
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:20,540
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

368
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:27,160
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand

369
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:34,380
That strange feeling I had back then

370
00:24:34,380 --> 00:24:39,580
So I walked along the arcade street's tiles

371
00:24:39,580 --> 00:24:45,360
stepping only on the black ones

372
00:24:47,860 --> 00:24:53,480
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

373
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:57,660
the politicians with
their self-important faces

374
00:24:57,660 --> 00:25:00,940
and that pesky old lady
who's a thorn in your side

375
00:25:00,940 --> 00:25:06,560
Turn at that corner over there

376
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:11,780
You can meet everyone, everyone

377
00:25:12,340 --> 00:25:16,520
That's Kameari

378
00:25:17,420 --> 00:25:19,860
It's surely Kameari

379
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:24,900
Everyone, come on over to our town!

380
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:26,520
Thank you

381
00:25:31,080 --> 00:25:34,360
Matoi's hidden memory on Kanda Hijiri Bridge

382
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:41,700
the first love Matoi, still a high school girl,
kept waiting for on the bridge through rainy and snowy days

383
00:25:42,320 --> 00:25:45,160
Next time: Hijiri Bridge, Hakusen Nagashi

384
00:25:45,740 --> 00:25:47,080
By the way, it's my time to shine

385
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:59,420
Everyone, come on over to our town!

386
00:26:00,940 --> 00:26:01,660
Start!

